      "goal_step": 1,
      "title": "Identify the domain and range of a function defined on a finite set",
      "skill": "conditions",
      "question": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Let the function \\(f : \\{1, 2, 3, 4\\} \\to \\mathbb{Z}\\) be defined by the rule"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "f(x) = 2x + 1",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 63,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Determine the domain, codomain, and range of \\(f\\)."
        }
      ],
      "answer": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "The domain is the input set: \\(\\{1, 2, 3, 4\\}\\)."
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "\\text{Codomain} = \\mathbb{Z}",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 63,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "The range is the set of outputs:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "f(1) = 3, \\quad f(2) = 5, \\quad f(3) = 7, \\quad f(4) = 9",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 63,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Thus, the range is \\(\\{3, 5, 7, 9\\}\\)."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
        "page": 63,
        "line_start": null,
        "line_end": null,
        "quote": null
      }
    },
    {
      "goal_step": 2,
      "title": "Determine if given functions are equal with differing domains",
      "skill": "comparison",
      "question": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Consider the following functions:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "f_1 : \\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}, \\quad f_1(x) = x - 1",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 64,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "g_1 : \\mathbb{R} \\setminus \\{0\\} \\to \\mathbb{R}, \\quad g_1(x) = \\frac{x^2 - 1}{x}",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 64,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Determine which of the functions \\(f_1, g_1\\) are equal."
        }
      ],
      "answer": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Note that \\(g_1\\) is undefined at \\(x = 0\\)."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "For \\(x \\neq 0\\), simplify"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "\\frac{x^2 - 1}{x} = \\frac{(x-1)(x+1)}{x} = x + 1 - \\frac{1}{x}",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 64,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Since \\(f_1(x) = x - 1\\) differs from this expression, even where defined, they are not equal."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Their domains differ and their formulas do not agree pointwise, so \\(f_1 \\neq g_1\\)."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
        "page": 64,
        "line_start": null,
        "line_end": null,
        "quote": null
      }
    },
    {
      "goal_step": 3,
      "title": "Prove a function from integers to integers is injective",
      "skill": "why_justification",
      "question": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Define a function \\(f : \\mathbb{Z} \\to \\mathbb{Z}\\) by"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "f(m) = 3m + 5",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 65,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Prove that \\(f\\) is injective."
        }
      ],
      "answer": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Suppose \\(f(m_1) = f(m_2)\\) for some \\(m_1, m_2 \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\). Then"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "3m_1 + 5 = 3m_2 + 5",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 65,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Subtract 5 from both sides:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "3m_1 = 3m_2",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 65,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Divide both sides by 3:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "m_1 = m_2",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 65,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Thus, \\(f\\) is injective because equal outputs imply equal inputs."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
        "page": 65,
        "line_start": null,
        "line_end": null,
        "quote": null
      }
    },
    {
      "goal_step": 4,
      "title": "Determine if a multi-variable function from integers to integers is bijective",
      "skill": "application",
      "question": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Consider the function \\(f : \\mathbb{Z} \\times \\mathbb{Z} \\to \\mathbb{Z} \\times \\mathbb{Z}\\) defined by"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "f(m,n) = (2m + n, m - n)",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 65,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Determine whether \\(f\\) is injective, surjective, and bijective. Justify your answers."
        }
      ],
      "answer": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "To prove injectivity, suppose "
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "f(m,n) = f(a,b)",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 65,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Thus,"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "(2m + n, m - n) = (2a + b, a - b)",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 65,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "From the first coordinate:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "2m + n = 2a + b",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 65,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "From the second coordinate:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "m - n = a - b",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 65,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Add the two equations:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "(2m + n) + (m - n) = (2a + b) + (a - b) \\implies 3m = 3a \\implies m = a",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 65,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Substitute back to the second equation:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "m - n = a - b \\implies a - n = a - b \\implies n = b",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 65,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Hence, \\((m,n) = (a,b)\\) and \\(f\\) is injective."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "To prove surjectivity, let \\((p,q) \\in \\mathbb{Z} \\times \\mathbb{Z}\\) be arbitrary. We must solve:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "2m + n = p, \\quad m - n = q",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 65,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Add the two equations:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "(2m + n) + (m - n) = p + q \\implies 3m = p + q \\implies m = \\frac{p + q}{3}",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 65,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Substitute back to solve for \\(n\\):"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "latex": "m - n = q \\implies n = m - q = \\frac{p + q}{3} - q = \\frac{p - 2q}{3}",
          "display": true,
          "source": {
            "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
            "page": 65,
            "line_start": null,
            "line_end": null,
            "quote": null
          },
          "original_latex": null,
          "change": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Since \\(m, n\\) must be integers, \\(f\\) is surjective onto \\(\\{(p,q) \\in \\mathbb{Z}^2 : p+q \\equiv 0 \\mod 3\\}\\) only."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Thus, \\(f\\) is not surjective onto all of \\(\\mathbb{Z} \\times \\mathbb{Z}\\) and hence not bijective."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "document_id": "ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff",
        "page": 65,
        "line_start": null,
        "line_end": null,
        "quote": null
      }
    }
